  "raw_text": "Step 1: Observe that the sequence alternates between adding and subtracting consecutive integers starting from 1 to 100.\n\nStep 2: Group the terms into pairs of the form (odd number) - (next even number). For example, the first pair is \\(1 - 2\\), the second is \\(3 - 4\\), and so on up to \\(99 - 100\\).\n\nStep 3: Each pair can be simplified as follows: \\(n - (n+1) = n - n - 1 = -1\\). Therefore, each pair contributes \\(-1\\) to the sum.\n\nStep 4: Determine the number of such pairs. Since we start from 1 and go up to 100, there are 50 pairs (because 100/2 = 50).\n\nStep 5: Multiply the number of pairs by the contribution of each pair: \\(50 \\times (-1) = -50\\).\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{-50}<|im_end|>",
